1.0.1-snapshot
  HITCHES, a shared COST table with caused-by attribution, and panel fixes
    HITCHES is a new tab. It records the time of each rendered frame with a CPU capture in the same run. If the game stutters, a single capture names the code that ran in the slow frames.
    CPU, MEM and HITCHES now share a COST table, where a mod is charged for the time in its code and for the vanilla or engine work it called.
    Tables keep their headers in place, INSTRUMENT has a filter, and time in a loadstring chunk books to the script that ran it.

  HITCHES
    - Added HITCHES, a capture of each rendered frame's time with a CPU capture in the same run.
      The report gives the median, mean, p95, p99 and 1% low, the worst frames, and whether the hitches repeat on a fixed interval.
      In the panel you get a frame-time timeline, the rhythm, the worst-frame table and what ran in the hitch frames. While it records, the corner banner shows the live frame time and fps.
    - Added a SpeedScope .folded of the hitch frames' stacks, written at stop.

  COST
    - Added the COST table on CPU, MEM and HITCHES. Each function is a row with Own, the time in its code, Caused, the vanilla or engine work it made run, and Cost, the sum.
      A mod is charged for what its callbacks, timers and scheme functions caused. A wrapper or a callback hook is passed over and named on the vanilla row.
      Heavy Anomaly code keeps a separate row at full weight, and the Cost column adds up to 100%.
    - Changed the 4 BY views into one Group by on the COST table, by function, script or mod.
    - Changed the VM-state split, the engine C entry points, Fold baseline and Parallel GC to sit under an Advanced fold.
    - Fixed time inside a loadstring chunk booking to "loadstring". It now books to the script that ran it.
    - Fixed 5 scripts of the 2026 modded exes booking as another mod's code. They now book to the modded exes.

  Publish
    - Added Publish to the footer. It commits the masked page to pages/jitprofiler.html in your GitHub repo through xlibs xnet, with no exe, and the game waits 10 s at most.
      The repo, branch and token last for the session only.

  Panel
    - Changed the tables to keep their headers in place while scrolling, with each percentage beside its bar.
    - Added a Filter box to INSTRUMENT.
    - Fixed hint text that was hard to read, and a locked tab or a disabled Start that lit up while a capture ran.

  Update check
    - Added an update check. The mod asks GitHub for a newer release and shows it at the foot of the MCM page and in a daily PDA message.
      Check for update on the MCM page asks right away.

1.0.0
  CPU and allocation sampling, instrumentation, callbacks, per-mod attribution, the panel
    JitProfiler samples the whole modpack at near-zero cost through jit.profile and jit.allocprof, engine primitives built for it in the modded exes.
    INSTRUMENT times every call of a chosen script set, CALLBACKS times every handler, and each cost names the mod that owns the script.
    The in-game panel on F11 runs every capture, masks other authors' names, and saves the masked captures as a local page.

  CPU and MEM
    - Added the CPU profile over jit.profile, with the VM-state split of JIT, interpreter, C, GC and compiler, and ranked views by mod, script, leaf and root.
    - Added the allocation profile over jit.allocprof. It counts the exact bytes for each function, with the same views.
    - Added per-mod attribution. A mod or script ranks by Total, anywhere on the stack, with Own for the innermost frame.
      A mod serving a stock-named file is flagged as an override of that file. Frames from the modded exes overlay and from engine C carry separate labels.
    - Added the deepest stack each capture recorded and how often a stack reached the depth cap. An under-counted Total shows at a glance.
    - Added Fold, which drops the vanilla baseline and leaves only mod cost.

  INSTRUMENT
    - Added INSTRUMENT, which wraps every function of a chosen script set and times each call, own and total, with the engine C included.
      Avg, min and max per call are sortable columns, with per-mod subtotals and a call graph of callers and callees.
      The BROWSE modlist adds a single script or a whole mod, searchable by mod or script name.

  CALLBACKS
    - Added CALLBACKS, which times every registered handler over the make_callback dispatch, ranked by own time with its callback and owning mod.
      If you only care about some callbacks, its picker narrows the capture to them.

  Panel
    - Added the in-game panel, opened from the ImGui menu bar under JitProfiler. It carries Start and Stop for each capture, a ranked table per view, and the callers and callees of a selected frame.
      A corner banner marks a live capture.
    - Added the panel Settings for the session: sample interval, stack depth, auto-snapshot threshold, auto-stop and fold. A console argument overrides one capture.
    - Added auto-stop, which ends a running capture after a set time and writes its report. This is a safety limit for the allocation profile, which holds the JIT off until the capture ends.
    - Added Anonymize, which masks every third-party mod and script name in the panel and in every export, letters and digits to #.
      A saved keep-list of patterns, 3 letters or more matched from the start of a name, keeps your own mods readable.
    - Added Save page, which writes the retained captures as one masked page to appdata/logs. You share this page by hand, because JitProfiler makes no network request.

  Reports
    - Added ASCII text reports to appdata/logs with a summary header, and a SpeedScope flamegraph per capture, each under a timestamped name.
    - Added start_cpu(interval_ms, depth) and start_alloc(depth) on the console, to set the sample rate and stack depth of one capture.

  MCM
    - Added the MCM about page, with Show in ImGui overlay to take JitProfiler off the F11 menu bar.

  Compatibility
    - Added the load check. Without xlibs or the modded exes the game stops with a message naming what to install, and the log records the build.
    - Added the capability guard. On an exe without the profiler primitives the commands print the build they need and skip the capture.
